    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Originally called Nacimiento, Cuba was abandoned due to frontier Indian tribe raids before being resettled in the late 1870s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cubanm.gov/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Cuba sits in the high desert at an elevation of 6,900 feet, skirting the picturesque Sierra Nacimiento.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cubanm.gov/visitor-information/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Known as Copper City, Cuba once thrived on an economy fueled by oil, gas, timber, and copper mining.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cubanm.gov/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The National Christmas Tree was harvested from the Santa Fe National Forest near Cuba in 2005 and 2019.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
